# Copy to `.env` beside this file and edit. `docker compose` reads `.env`
# from its own directory automatically, so run it from `docker/`:
#
#   cd docker
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   docker compose up -d
#   docker compose exec dev zsh
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This file is not: it is the documentation of what the
# compose file reads, so keep the two in step.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. The unprivileged account inside the image, and its numeric ids.
# There is deliberately **no default** for any of the three, here or in the
# Dockerfile: this account is a property of your machine, not of the project,
# and a default that is wrong for almost everyone is worse than none -- it
# works just well enough to write files owned by the wrong uid into the
# checkout you mounted, which you then cannot edit from outside the container.
#
# Fill these in from your own account:
#
#     echo "PRA_USER=$(id -un)"
#     echo "PRA_UID=$(id -u)"
#     echo "PRA_GID=$(id -g)"
#
# One value to avoid: uid **1000** is already taken inside the image by the
# Node base image's own `node` account, and two accounts sharing a numeric
# owner on a bind mount is its own kind of confusing.
#
# These are build args as well as runtime settings, so changing them needs
# `docker compose build`, not just a restart.
PRA_USER=your-login-name
PRA_UID=1001
PRA_GID=1001

# The checkout mounted at /workspace. Defaults to `..` -- the repository this
# file is in -- which is what you want when working in a clone. Point it at a
# git worktree or a second clone to run the container against that instead.
#PRA_WORKSPACE=/absolute/path/to/pr-review-agent

# Host directory for the container's ~/.claude. This is what persists the
# `claude` login, so a rebuild is not a re-authentication. Relative paths are
# resolved against docker/. Log in once with:
#
#     docker compose exec dev claude   # then /login
#
# A separate directory from your own ~/.claude by default, on purpose: the
# container runs the reviewer, and pointing it at your personal home would
# have it share settings and history with your interactive sessions.
#PRA_CLAUDE_HOME=./claude

# The GitHub PAT, with read and write on pull requests. Only `host check` and
# `daemon start` need it; the test suite and the linters do not, and never
# reach the network. Leave it unset here and export it in your shell instead
# if you would rather it not sit in a file.
#GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

# The container's name: what `docker exec -it <name> bash` takes. Also its
# hostname. Set it if you run more than one of these.
#PRA_CONTAINER_NAME=pr-review-agent-dev

# Compose's project name, which prefixes the network. Set it per checkout to
# run two of these side by side -- together with a distinct
# PRA_CONTAINER_NAME, which is the one that would actually collide.
#PRA_PROJECT_NAME=pr-review-agent

# Which image tag to run. Build a candidate as `:tmp` and point one checkout
# at it without disturbing the `:latest` everything else uses.
#PRA_IMAGE_TAG=latest
